These data files have two overlapping deletions, both with junctions.
Currently the test only finds the majority one, but they could be used
to test improved polymorphism prediction algorithms.

tmv-plasmid-origin-extra-base.gbk is tmv-plasmid.gbk rotated so that its base
8501 is base 1 (putting the origin in a region the reads cover), with one extra
T added at the end. The TTT run that spans the new origin becomes TTTT, so the
reads show a 1-bp deletion ON the origin that leaves no missing coverage: it is
supported only by a junction from base 1 to base (length - 1). No annotation.
